    "result": "I implemented `can_book` and `merge_intervals` in `solution.py` to match `spec.md`, and added 10 tests in `tests/test_solution.py`. All 10 pass with `python -m pytest -q tests`.\n\n- **`can_book`:** it raises `ValueError` for `end <= start` or a negative buffer. It then rejects bookings that cross midnight, run over 4 hours, or fall outside open hours. Finally it checks each existing booking, requiring the new one to start at least the buffer after it ends or end at least the buffer before it starts.\n- **`merge_intervals`:** it validates every interval first. It then sorts a copy of the list and merges overlapping or touching intervals, so the input is not modified.\n- **Tests:** they cover the exact boundaries (4 hours, open and close times, back-to-back bookings, buffers), the `ValueError` cases, and that `merge_intervals` leaves its input unchanged.",
